            <ArticleTitle>[Severe asthma due to an esophageal foreign body in a child].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1047-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 4-year-old boy had infantile bronchial asthma resistant to treatment. He was referred for a febrile respiratory distress which led to the diagnosis of periesophagus mediastinis mass with erosion of both contiguous vertebral discs. The oesophagogram showed a foreign body in an esophageal diverticulum. After its extraction, all pulmonary symptoms disappeared.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
